→ ×1.00 | ≈ −2385 | ≈ −1745 | ≈ −4130 |\n| 0 | ×1.15 | ≈ −2605 | ≈ −1885 | ≈ −4490 |\n| 4 | ×1.25 | ≈ −4145 | ≈ −2920 | ≈ −7060 |\n\nGoing from candidate 1 to candidate 2 saves about 440 in lost sales for product 0 and about 400 for product 1. But it costs about 590 and 500 respectively in purchases and holding, so the move is a net loss for both products.\n\n**Batch plans (3 and 6).**\n- **Candidate 6** orders every 2 days at about ×1.1. It saves 12 × 27 = 324 in order fees, but carrying the second day's stock overnight costs about 510 in holding. On top of that, deliveries of ~185 units plus the buffer press against the 220-unit warehouse limit.\n- **Candidate 3** orders every 3 days. It saves 432 in fees but pays about 1000 in extra holding. Deliveries of 200+ units (215 on day 11) overflow the warehouse, and the excess is lost.\n\n**Robustness.** Demand is skewed upward: occasional spikes can't be cheaply covered by a small buffer, while buffers cost money every day. That favours the lean plans. Candidate 1 is ahead of candidate 2 by about 240 and well ahead of everything else."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 355, "cache_read_input_tokens": 6882, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 355}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-25T18:54:52.874Z", "request_id": "req_011CgPTee4SHdtRxJcuFyfT2"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01TsNQM3tNpTHMYdezU4Kds8", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, 